      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1899-01-27_WidnesExaminer_art0062" n="art0062">
        <head>WORTH YOUR ATTENTION,</head>
        <p>WORTH YOUR ATTENTION,</p>
        <p>Every person's future is to a certain extent in his own hand. Many a future which might have been bril- last has been darkened by lack of timely preparation to meet the exigencies and changes which occur in every day life. Many a home which might have been glad- dened by life andhealth, and conafort,has been saddened by poverty, illness, and death, in many cases wholly preventable. There ate, indeed, few that do not feel the system needs recruiting after tbe trying feeling of lassitude, with others, " not quite up to the mark." "a god of all over sinking feeling," "too weak to do any- thing about the house," "these recurring headaches," "no appetite for my food," etc. These, and a dozen others, are common expressions which all point to the urgent need of some good tonic mixture, a reliable me• dicine of established reputation and of proved virtue. There are several tonic mixtures to be bad, but none which have been so uniformly successful as Gwilym Evans' Quinine Bitters; it has never been known to fail. It's always the same, there can be no mistake about it. The careful preparation and a manipulation of manufacture under the most stringent rules, assures the certainty that Gwilym Evans' Qainine Bitters, the Vegetable Tonic, is always efficacious and geouinely successful in all eases of Incligestion,Weakness,Nervous- :less, Low Spirits, Sleeplessness, Dyspepsia, Liver Corn. plaints, Neuralgia, and Influeen. We claim that Gwilym Evans's Quinine Bitters is a General Benefactor of Suf- fering Humanity. Hundrel 3of testimonials prove this, coming from all classes of the community. Pain is no respector of persons, be advised, try Gwilym Evans' Quinine Bitters,a sovereign remedy for various ailments, for rich and poor alike. When you buy Gwilym Evans' Quinine Bitters, you get what you think you get, abso- lutely the Tonic of Natures own providing, comprised of the beneficient properties contained in Sarsaparilla, Saffron, Geeitian, Burdock, Lavender, and Dendelien in addition to Quinine. It is not so much what you pay for a thing, but what you get for what you pay. Don't listen to the "Just as sod" argument, there is no Tonic " Just as good" as Gwilyin Evans' Quinine Bitters, it stands supreme. To prevent disappointment, above al thieves see that you get the right article, with the name "Gwilym Evans "on Label, Stamp, and Bottle. without -which none is genuine. Sold everywhere in bottles 2s. 93. and 48.63. each, but should any difficulty be ex- perienced in procuring Gwilym Evans' Quinine Bitters, it will be forwarded carriage free, for the above prices, by the Sole Proprietors : The Quinine Bitters Manufac- turing Compsny, Limited, Llanelly, South Walee.</p>
