        <head>SENSATIONAL NEWS.</head>
        <p>SENSATIONAL NEWS.</p>
        <p>Some time ago the Eilisr press anno once,' the dis- covery of curative treeten,nt for the deaf aed dumb. This pieee of sensa!lonal news, however, has nit ye-, been confirmed, se it will be as well to wait for more ample details bef ore accepting it as cerreet. But if doubts may be entertained cn the sabjelt, it is at least incontestable that wher !e'er D eafness is not col genital, that is to s iv, when it does not date from birth, it is quite curable, unless in very few eases. As proof of thie statement we quote the undermentioned cure, which should prove absolutely conclusive Join Proud, fifty-eieht years of age, had suffered hr eight years from av Ty grave aural affec- tion. The tympanic membrane had gradu Ally become thick and lost its elasticity, so ths transmission of sound was no longer nessible, on wesount of the rigidity of the tympanum. The deafness was complete, and the noises in the ear were incessant. The petieet was treated by co:respendence, and exactly four weeks after commenc- ing the treatment was completely curet Intimating his reenvery, he wrote as follows from 16, Milton-place, Gravesend:— " I am happy to inform you that I am dill improving in my hearing. I can now h iar any whisper across the room. I can hear a clock tick from five or six yards away. You can make any use of mg testimonial to let the public know, and I shall be happy to answer any question and bring witnesses to prove what you have dine." It should les stated that this remarkable cure was effected by the tasatrnent of the Denuet Institute. We would strongly re.eemmend all our readers who suffer fr om complaints of the Bar, Tnroat, and Nose to write to the !Amager of thst medical establishment at 72. Re- gent's Park Road, London. N.W., for a copy of the "Newspaper for the Deaf," which is forwarded free on application. In this publication will be found very in- ter-sting information both as to the method emoloved in the treatment of these comp!aints, and the successful results obtained in several hundreds of ca .es.</p>
