      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1899-01-27_WidnesExaminer_art0081" n="art0081">
        <head>BEWSEY WARD CONTEST.</head>
        <p>THE BEWSEY WARD CONTEST.</p>
        <p>The municipal contest which takes place in this ward on Monday is to be fought and decided be- tween the two former candidates, Messrs. Malkin and Rogers,without the intervention of any other candidates. This is perhaps as well under the cir; cumstances. The ward is being well canvassed by both parties. Polling will take place at 93, Hoyle- street, and Dannett-street schoolroom, from 8 a.m to 8 p.m. on the day named—Monday. Mr Malkin has been proposed by Mr. F. R. Roberts seconded by Mr Richard Travis, and. supported by Messrs ,John Waring. William Ford, Thomas Field, John Ridge, William Ryder, John Coyne, James Harris and tnock Sheargold ; while in a second paper he is proposed by Mr James Ash- ton and seconded by Mr Edward Hardman. On Monday last a little before 5 o'dock Mr Rogers handed in his nominations. His proposers and. seconders are as follows:—Proposeri:Ed win Wright, William Moffatt, James McLean, John Tomkinson Grindrod, Thomas Tickle. Ralph Barlow,John Black- burn, Oeorge Herbert, Thomas Partidge, Charles Frederick Eaton. Seconders: Messrs Thomas Law- rinson, Thomas Stokes, James Winall, James Kenyon, John Plinston, George Haddock, Josiah Richards, Henry Harrison, Eh Gough, and George Plump.</p>
      </div>
