        <p>Mr. Malley said he had been app:oacned. lev another landlord in town to reme7e the headquarters of the club from it* present able to the 14,gin Arms Hotel. He had had a promize of a good subscription from Mr. S. Hutoninson, and also of a good bowling prize, and Mr. Airey waull also in-erease his subscription. He therefore moved thot the headquarters of the c'ub be in future the Legb Arms Hotel.—rhis was not seconded and it fell through. A. vote of thanks to the Chairman broueut the meet- ing to a close.</p>
